WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.000
If you've ever tried Ethereum, you've paid a gas fee.

2
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:14.000
Most people assume it's a tax the blockchain charges.

3
00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:17.667
It's not. Here's what's actually happening.

4
00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:24.000
Every action on Ethereum requires computation.

5
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Validators run the computers that process and validate every tx.

6
00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:46.000
Gas fee = your payment to them for that work.

7
00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:52.667
High demand = everyone competing for block space = fees spike.

8
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Layer 2s bundle transactions to make fees dramatically cheaper.

9
00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:05.000
Gas fees are not a bug. They are a feature of decentralization.

10
00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:08.667
Learn Web3 fundamentals at 0xverse Academy.

